inline std::unordered_set<const NVSDK_NGX_Handle*> block_classified_fg_handles;
// The game's create-time contract per intercepted DLSS/DLSSD create: the
// state DeriveFeatureState read from the CREATE block.  Both records above
// describe the GAME's features and live as long as they do - cleared by the
// release hooks and by the destruction of the device NR ran on, never by an
// NR teardown.  A non-resize swapchain destroy or a device-face change tears
// NR down (`features`) while the game keeps its handle, and a title that
// evaluates through its own parameter block (AllocateParameters per call is
// legal, and the NGX helpers set only evaluate fields) never sends IsHDR,
// AutoExposure, MVLowRes, DepthInverted or the create guide dims again:
